WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.825
Measuring the current is half the job.

2
00:00:03.075 --> 00:00:09.125
The other half is beating it: finding the course to steer so that you travel along the line you want.

3
00:00:09.375 --> 00:00:12.975
You do it with a small drawing called a current diagram.

4
00:00:13.225 --> 00:00:16.400
Look at the diagram, and take it in three steps.

5
00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:17.925
One.

6
00:00:18.175 --> 00:00:22.325
Draw your intended track, from your start toward your destination.

7
00:00:22.575 --> 00:00:23.875
Two.

8
00:00:24.125 --> 00:00:28.725
From the start, draw the current: its set, and its drift for one hour.

9
00:00:28.975 --> 00:00:30.350
Three.

10
00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:38.225
From the end of that current line, set your dividers to your boat speed, and swing an arc until it cuts the intended track.

11
00:00:39.225 --> 00:00:41.375
Now read your two answers.

12
00:00:41.625 --> 00:00:46.700
The line from the end of the current to that crossing point is your course to steer.

13
00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:52.600
And the distance along the track, from the start to the crossing point, is your speed made good.

14
00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:54.475
Current first.

15
00:00:54.725 --> 00:00:56.425
Then your speed.

16
00:00:56.675 --> 00:00:58.675
Always in that order.
